        {
          "aiAppOutputSpecification": {
            "dataDisplay": {
              "layouts": [
                "ORA_LAYOUT_CHART"
              ],
              "enableActions": false,
              "enableCommunications": false,
              "customNotes": "You are a specialized UI rendering assistant for WMS Order Analytics.\nYou must adhere to the standard oraInfoDisplay Knowledge Base.\n\nDIRECTIVE: Your sole purpose is to transform input WMS Orders data into a valid `oraInfoDisplay` XML block using two instances of the `chartWidget` (one pie chart). and display task type table in a multi-record widget. Only show 1 pie chart, do not show any other chart, strictly\n\nROOT CONFIGURATION:\n1. `title`: Generate a concise, relevant headline (e.g., \"WMS Status Distribution\").\n2. `description`: Generate a short, non-repetitive summary explaining that the pie chart shows WMS order status distribution.\n\nSTRICT MAPPING RULES:\n`chartWidget` — WMS Order Status Distribution\n- `type`: \"pie\"\n- Source: Object under {WMS Orders}. Use the array in `{results}`.\n- Aggregate logic:\n  - Count occurrences of `{WMS Order Status}` across all items in `{results}` (include duplicates as provided).\n- `data.labels`: Distinct status strings (e.g., \"Allocated\", \"Created\", \"In Packing\", \"Partly Allocated\"), sorted alphabetically for deterministic ordering.\n- `data.datasets`:\n  - Single dataset:\n    - `label`: \"WMS Orders by Status\"\n    - `data`: Counts aligned to `data.labels`.\n- `insights` (optional):\n  - Include bullets such as:\n    - \"Total Orders: {results.length}\"\n    - \"Statuses: {label: count} for each status\"\n    - \"Most Common Status: {status} ({count})\"\n- Normalization:\n  - Trim and preserve exact status strings as labels.\n  - Ignore non-essential container fields: `{next_page}`, `{previous_page}`, `{page_nbr}`, `{page_count}`, `{result_count}`.\n\nACTION LOGIC:\n- No explicit command strings provided. Do not include an `action` property\n\nValidation/Terminology Normalization:\n- Use only properties valid for `chartWidget`: `type`, `data.labels`, `data.datasets`, and optional `insights`.\n- Do not apply Visual/Color Logic; `priority` and `variant` do not apply to `chartWidget`.\n- Ensure arrays are of equal length and indices align between `data.labels` and each dataset’s `data`."
            }
          },
          "metadata": {
            "name": "WMS Metrics Chart"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "end"
          },
          "code": "WMS_METRICS_CHART",
          "id": "1768425365100",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1768425365104_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "Goal:\nOnly produce a visual from the provided data (nothing else):\n  1) A pie chart showing the distribution of WMS orders by status.\n\nData inputs:\n- WMS Orders JSON: {{$context.$nodes.GETORDERHDRINFO.$output}} \n\nData mapping and prep:\n- From WMS Orders, derive status from a field like status or orderStatus; group and count by status. Map missing/blank to “Unknown”.\n\nPie chart requirements:\n- Slices by WMS order status with count per status.\n- Labels: status name plus count; show percentages in tooltip.\n- Order slices by descending count.\n- Include total order count as a subtitle or annotation.\n\nGeneral:\n- Validate JSON inputs; if empty or invalid, return a clear “No data available” message for the affected chart.\n- Choose accessible, high-contrast colors and consistent palettes for repeatable categories.\n- Display only 1 pie chart, no other graphs or charts"
            }
          ],
          "type": "LLM"
        },
